# Release notes for v0.225.45

File: openOODA/audit/release_notes/RELEASE_NOTES_v0.225.45.oot

Logline: aarch64_main.oo now uses the in-process AST path (v0.225.43 was the process-spawn form) and surfaces actual compile errors instead of the silent "compile failed" message.

Setup: ooda.pkg version=0.225.45. Tag v0.225.45.

Beats:
  1. oodac/aarch64_main.oo main signature changed from (p: &ProcessCap, fs: &FsCap, args) to (sys: &SysCap, fs: &FsCap, args). The AST path now calls aarch64_emit_direct_elf_binary(sys, src, out_path) in-process; no shell-out, no oodac.aarch64.ast dependency.
  2. oodac/aarch64_emit_elf.oo: aarch64_emit_direct_elf_binary now prints the actual Err message from aarch64_compile_to_elf before returning false.
  3. Verified end-to-end: oodac.aarch64 --ast-emit-aarch64 fixtures/aarch64_hello.oo /tmp/h.bin -> ELF64, qemu-aarch64 prints "Hello", exit 0.
  4. Verified error surfacing: oodac.aarch64 --ast-emit-aarch64 fixtures/aarch64_closure.oo /tmp/c.bin now prints `ERR\tast-emit-aarch64\tERR\taarch64_compile_program_elf\tbad_item\t@413\tb=40` instead of the silent `compile failed`. This identifies the closure as a known AST path limitation.

What this proves:
  * The aarch64 side has a single binary with both paths in-process (no oodac.aarch64.ast dependency).
  * Compile errors from the AST path are now actionable: users see the underlying error, not a generic "compile failed".

Out of scope: closures (still rejected as bad_item by aarch64_compile_program_elf). The aarch64_xclosure.oo modules exist in std/ but the AST path does not yet lower them.
